# Conway's Game of Life (the pack is packs/life) on a board with no edge: every
# cell is soil, and each starts alive with a chance of 3 in 8, else dead, drawn
# from the seed. One generation per tick, 8 a second at 1x.
#
#   make run ARGS="play saves/life --scenario scenarios/life.scenario"
#   make run ARGS="run saves/life 100 --scenario scenarios/life.scenario"   # 100 generations, headless, timed
#
# `size` is only what is made at the start; the camera starts in its middle.
# The rest is made the first time the camera comes near it, fresh soup from the
# same seed, so the board goes on as far as you scroll. As everywhere on this
# engine, only the part around the camera runs: what you leave behind is saved
# (about half a megabyte a chunk) and waits, frozen, until you come back.
# `play` saves on quit and reopens saves/life where you left it: delete that
# directory to start over. wasd scrolls, space pauses, `.` steps a generation,
# `[` and `]` change the speed, `-` zooms out.
#
# Another seed is another soup, and the shares set the density. They must add
# up to exactly 1 for every cell to be on the board: eighths do (see RULES.md).
rules ../packs/life
seed 1
size 512 512                                          # 262,144 cells in 64 chunks
terrain water_level 0 rock_on_soil 0 rock_on_water 0  # all soil: nothing but the board
start alive 3 / 8
start dead  5 / 8
